    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABHPP7hQ",
      "title": "interop: specify per-message expiry and SuperchainETHBridge refunds",
      "author": "karlfloersch",
      "number": 960,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nSpecifies per-message interop expiry and `SuperchainETHBridge` refunds, implemented in ethereum-optimism/optimism#23259.\n\nA destination chain's sequencer can refuse to relay an interop message forever, and executing messages cannot be included through deposits. Once the expiry window passes, the message can never be relayed. This specifies how the source chain learns that, using only a withdrawal and a deposit, so applications can undo the send.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **New `interop/message-expiry.md`:**\n  - the flow (export on the destination, relay through L1, expire on the source);\n  - `L1CrossDomainMessenger.relayUndeliveredMessage`;\n  - the safety argument: not relayed at destination time `t`, and `t` past the send time plus `EXPIRY_PERIOD`, means it can never be relayed;\n  - activation conditions.\n- **`interop/predeploys.md`, `L2ToL2CrossDomainMessenger`:**\n  - adds `sentMessageTimestamps`, `expiredMessages`, `expireMessage` and its invariants, and `EXPIRY_PERIOD` (8 days, at least the expiry window);\n  - rejects the `L2CrossDomainMessenger` and `L2ToL1MessagePasser` as message targets on send and relay;\n  - removes `resendMessage`.\n- **`interop/predeploys.md`, new `UndeliveredMessageExporter`** predeploy at `0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000030`.\n- **`interop/superchain-eth-bridge.md`:** `refundETH`, the `RefundETH` event, invariant iSEB-004 (refund only for expired sends, at most once) and assumption aSEB-004.\n- **`interop/derivation.md`:**\n  - a dependency set must not configure an expiry window above `EXPIRY_WINDOW` (7 days), and nodes and the proof program must reject one that does;\n  - the security note now points to message expiry instead of resending.\n- **Navigation:** linked from `SUMMARY.md` and the interop overview.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T01:53:00Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 274,
      "deletions": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABGuHwlw",
      "title": "specs: make airgap delays configurable per chain",
      "author": "zkfrov",
      "number": 954,
      "body": "## Context\n\nThe per-chain air gap (optimism-private#684) moves `PROOF_MATURITY_DELAY_SECONDS`,\n`DISPUTE_GAME_FINALITY_DELAY_SECONDS` and the `DelayedWETH` delay from implementation\nimmutables to per-chain values set at initialization and adjustable by the L1 ProxyAdmin\nowner within bounds. The specs still describe them as immutables.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `fault-proof/stage-one/optimism-portal.md`: proof maturity delay is per chain and read at\n  check time. Finalization condition stated as\n  `max(provenAt + proofMaturityDelay, resolvedAt + finalityDelay)`. Adds the bound getters,\n  the setter and aOP-004 for portals sharing an `ETHLockbox`.\n- `fault-proof/stage-one/anchor-state-registry.md`: same for the finality delay. Notes it is\n  shared by every chain and game type using the registry.\n- `experimental/contracts/dispute/delayed-weth.md`: same for the withdrawal delay. Also\n  updates `initialize` and pause lookup to the `ETHLockbox` model.\n- `protocol/configurability.md`: the three requirements become ranges with the L1 ProxyAdmin\n  owner as administrator.\n- `bridge-integration.md`, `bond-incentives.md`, `fault-dispute-game.md`, `zk-dispute-game.md`:\n  cross-references updated.\n\nSetter and getter names are provisional until optimism-private#686 and #692 open.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-05T13:54:14Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-07T21:41:09Z",
      "additions": 217,
      "deletions": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABGKbamA",
      "title": "interop: update specs for pause based on the lockbox",
      "author": "0xiamflux",
      "number": 951,
      "body": "## Context\r\nSince ethereum-optimism/optimism#22760, pause state resolves through the `ETHLockbox` rather than a per-chain `SystemConfig`. Three specs still described the old model.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- **`protocol/superchain-config.md`**: add `isLocalOrGlobalPaused(address)`, true\r\n  when the global or the identifier-scoped pause is active. Clarify that `paused(address)` is identifier-scoped only, and that the no-argument `paused()` is the legacy global-only overload.\r\n- **`interop/eth-lockbox.md`**: `initialize` takes `(ISuperchainConfig, IOptimismPortal[])`, `paused()` returns `superchainConfig.isLocalOrGlobalPaused(address(this))`, and `superchainConfig` is stored rather than read through a `SystemConfig`. Adds the missing `guardian` getter.\r\n- **`interop/optimism-portal.md`**: `paused()`, `superchainConfig()` and `guardian()` are served by the lockbox, and the shared lockbox address is the set's only pause identifier. Adds `DelayedWETH` to the shared-contract list.\r\n\r\nCloses #950 ",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T19:27:45Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 131,
      "deletions": 25
    }
